# Globe.gl Integration Implementation Plan

Replace the current "3D tilt" logic in `DeckGLMap.ts` with a dedicated `GlobeMap.ts` engine powered by `globe.gl`. This will allow for a true 3D globe view when "3D" mode is selected.

## Proposed Changes

### Core Engines

#### [NEW] [GlobeMap.ts](file:///d:/Dev/GLOBAL-INTELLIGENCE-AI-DASHBOARD/src/components/GlobeMap.ts)
Implementation of the 3D globe using the `globe.gl` library.
- Initializing the globe with topographic textures and starfield background.
- Implementing semi-transparent atmosphere and custom polygons/markers.
- Adding auto-rotation logic with idle resume (60s).

#### [NEW] [globe-render-settings.ts](file:///d:/Dev/GLOBAL-INTELLIGENCE-AI-DASHBOARD/src/services/globe-render-settings.ts)
Configuration for globe textures, colors, and performance settings.

### Components

#### [MODIFY] [MapContainer.ts](file:///d:/Dev/GLOBAL-INTELLIGENCE-AI-DASHBOARD/src/components/MapContainer.ts)
Update the container to manage three engines: `DeckGLMap` (2D), `GlobeMap` (3D), and `MapComponent` (Mobile fallback).
- Implement `switchToGlobe()` and `switchToFlat()` methods.
- Add `rehydrateActiveMap()` to sync data across engines during a switch.
- Update `toggle3DMode()` to trigger engine switching instead of camera tilt.

### Layout & Logic

#### [MODIFY] [panel-layout.ts](file:///d:/Dev/GLOBAL-INTELLIGENCE-AI-DASHBOARD/src/app/panel-layout.ts)
Ensure the `mapDimensionToggle` correctly calls the new `toggle3DMode` in `MapContainer`.

